I have a 4M system running Windows 3.1 and MS-DOS 6.  I am using the
DoubleSpace disk compression program.  Has anyone succesfully ran
nethack/386 UNDER WINDOWS on a similar system?

With my normal setup, I can run nethack just fine under DOS.  Once I
start Windows, I get an out-of-memory error, which makes absolutely
no sense, since virtual memory gives me *more* memory than under a
plain DOS session.

I even 1) removed all funky drivers from the Windows INI files, 2)
removed smartdrv from my setup, and 3) set up a pif file to lock *all*
memory for nethack.  This gave me more PHYSICAL memory free under a
DOS session from Windows than I have in my normal DOS setup (since
my normal DOS setup includes a 1M disk cache, etc.)  Still no go.

I can run nethack in about 2.5M from DOS, so why can't I run it with
6M virtual memory or 3M physical memory from Windows?  I also run a
few large, complex DPMI programs (such as Borland C++ 3.1), and I
have never had any problems like this with them.  What's the deal?


